From 22a53f898c1a9ef6167828cdd53c969ed72c2a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Stufflebeam <cpuchip@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 07:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] APPS: Babal in the registry, from stu32-arcade at ARCADE_PIN

Babal (the games seat's port of Christian Mauduit's public-domain game, its rules judged byte
for byte against babalcore and played end to end under apps.h v1) joins KEYS in app_registry[].
Its sources stay in cpuchip/stu32-arcade (PRIVATE) and are consumed the way casim consumes the
core: scripts/fetch-arcade.sh exports babal/ and app/ at ARCADE_PIN (94c821d) with git archive
from a local clone (ARCADE_REPO, default ../stu32-arcade) into build/arcade, never writing into
it. They build with -ffp-contract=off, which their oracle requires (allowing fused multiply-adds
turns its pins red); nothing else's flags change. device/standin/run.sh and device/reva/build.sh
run the export before the image build.

Checked on 0253776 in a scratch clone: make all and make test pass (rc 0); app_test 467/467 with
Babal registered; standin_test 349/349, 5 screens, rc 0 (run by hand before build/standin/ exists
it reports 344/349 and exits 1, its five PNG writes failing, with or without this patch); the
stand-in and Rev A images build (the one warning, dev_tone_of unused, is there without it too).

Written by arcade for soroban to apply (abacus #4545).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
